Package: quickkey
Architecture: all
# python3-tk is Debian's name for tkinter; python3 alone does not pull it in
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, python3, python3-tk
Recommends: xclip
Suggests: xsel, wl-clipboard
Description: hotkey menu of commands whose output goes to the clipboard
 quickkey pops up a small window listing commands from a config file.
 Pick one by clicking or typing, the command runs, and its standard
 output is placed on the system clipboard.
 .
 It is standard library Python with tkinter, plus an external clipboard
 helper (xclip, xsel or wl-copy), since Tk's own clipboard is dropped
 when the process exits.
 .
 A systemd user unit is included that keeps a hidden window resident, so
 the hotkey opens it in about 20ms instead of 60ms.
